(
        '19002',
        'Check the differences between count alerts of AML Close alerts report and job basket',
        'Discrepancy in closed alert counts — between January and April 16, 2025, only 157 alerts are recorded as closed, whereas monthly reports indicate closure of 595 alerts. Reported figures are inconsistent.',
        'Dears,    Based on our web session, please note that the difference you noticed in the number of closed alerts reported while the selected period is from (01 January 2025 to 16 April 2025). Within this timeframe, the actual total number of alerts that were closed is 180, but the exported report shows only 155.     This difference is due to how the system generates the report, it filters the closed alerts based on the End Date (which means is the date of the alert was actually closed). Alerts are only included in the report if their End Date falls within the selected period. So, if an alert was opened during the date range but its End Date is after 16 April 2025, it will not appear in the report, as shown in the picture below the total of the closed alerts:       Picture 2 below shows one of the alert workcase hold number (185847) was closed on 22-04-2025, which is after the date you mentioned.  This workflow information provides the alert details from the time it was opened until it was closed, including the relevant dates       To explain more clearly:    - For example, if an alert was opened on 04 April 2025 but closed on 17 April 2025, it will not appear in the report because the closing date is after 16 April. This means any alert that was closed after 16 April 2025, based on the filter applied will not be included in the report even if it was opened within the selected date range.    This is why you see only 155 alerts instead of 180 the missing alerts were closed after the date range you filtered for.    2. Regarding to the second part you mentioned: You stated that “whereas monthly reports indicate the closure of 595 alerts.” Could you please provide more details about this statement? Specifically, which reports you are referring to, the date range they cover, and how the total of 595 closed alerts was calculated. This information will help us better understand fully problem.',
