        'HELLO Mohammad.  We have issue of system not working when we login we got an error message.  See attached.  Thanks.  ________________________________________',
        'Dear Mgeni,    Based on our web session, kindly find below the status:      • Issue Reported by the customer: system not working.    • Status: Solved.    • Problem description: The BankBI & SAPBO stopped because the size of archives has reached the limit of 500 GB, in addition PBZ team has configured Oracle in the archive mode.         • Action Taken – recommended solution: Based on our web session, kindly be informed that the issue was resolved by increasing the related configuration to be 1 TB , restarting the SAPBO services & re-extracting the missing data.       Note: Based on our DBA feedback, kindly consider the following:  1- PBZ team must delete the unneeded archives under the following path /backup/archives/BANKBIPROD.  2- If archives reach 1 TB, the issue will appear again, and the instance might crash   Logs :    Reclaimable space = 23552  Available space = 0  Disk space limit = 536870912000  See trace file /u01/app/oracle/diag/rdbms/bankbiprod/BANKBIPROD/trace/BANKBIPROD_ora_11438.trc for usage information from V$RECOVERY_AREA_USAGE  2025-06-17T14:56:32.012130+03:00  Errors in file /u01/app/oracle/diag/rdbms/bankbiprod/BANKBIPROD/trace/BANKBIPROD_ora_11438.trc:  ORA-19809: limit exceeded for recovery files  ORA-19804: cannot reclaim 181564416 bytes disk space from 536870912000 bytes limit  NET (PID:11438): Error 19809 Creating archive log file to ''/backup/archives/BANKBIPROD/archivelog/2025_06_17/o1_mf_1_120715_%u_.arc''  NET (PID:11438): Stuck archiver: inactive mandatory LAD:1  NET (PID:11438): Stuck archiver condition declared  2025-06-17T14:56:32.028503+03:00  Errors in file /u01/app/oracle/diag/rdbms/bankbiprod/BANKBIPROD/trace/BANKBIPROD_ora_11438.trc:  ORA-16038: log 1 sequence# 120715 cannot be archived  ORA-19809: limit exceeded for recovery files  ORA-00312: online log 1 thread 1: ''/u01/app/oracle/oradata/BANKBIPROD/redo01.log''         Kindly check from your side and confirm to close this ticket.    Best Regards,',
