(
        '19262',
        'Check daily fill - JOR01',
        'Dear @Mohammad Abedrabbu ,    Kindly note the same issue appears again and JOR01 is empty, please connect with us urgently to avoid any issue on today fill.    Kind Regards,  Obieda omar  MIS (Management Information Systems) Officer  Arab Jordan Investment Bank   Tel: +962 6 550 7000 Ext. 2349  Mob: +962 776681381  e-Mail: obieda.omar@ajib.com  Website: www.ajib.com',
        'As of 17-July-2025, please find the ticket status:    Dear Obieda,    Based on our web session, kindly find below the status:      • Issue Reported by the customer: Check daily fill - JOR01.    • Status: Solved.    • Problem description: The ETL job was hanging at the EXECUTE_ALL_GOAML_PROCEDURES_AJIB procedure, which is the final step in the GOAML_PLAN ETL job.     • Action Taken – recommended solution: Based on our web session, kindly be informed that the issue was resolved by applying performance tuning to the EXECUTE_ALL_GOAML_PROCEDURES_AJIB procedure. Additional tuning was also performed on the FILL_PIO_FATCA_ALERTS procedure, which is the last procedure executed within EXECUTE_ALL_GOAML_PROCEDURES_AJIB. The overall execution time has now been reduced to approximately five (5) hours.  We plan to continue optimizing the FILL_PIO_FATCA_ALERTS procedure next week to further reduce its execution time. For now, we will consider this case closed.  Kindly check from your side and confirm to close this ticket.     Best Regards,     -------------------------------------------------------------------------    As of 16-July-2025, please find the ticket status:    Nader from the Modeling team has made multiple performance tuning adjustments to the FATCA engine procedures. We will evaluate the impact of these modifications tomorrow.    ------------------------------------------------------------------------    As of 15-July-2025 please find the ticket status:    Dear Obieda,  Good afternoon, I hope this email finds you well.    Kindly be informed that we have applied a performance tuning to the EXECUTE_ALL_GOAML_PROCEDURES_AJIB procedure, which is called at the final step of the GOAML_PLAN ETL job. However, there is still a performance issue with the final procedure before the ETL job completes, namely FILL_PIO_FATCA_ALERTS.    We are currently working to resolve the issue in collaboration with the Pio-Tech development team and expect to have it fixed by tomorrow.    We sincerely apologize for any inconvenience this may have caused, and truly appreciate your patience and understanding.    Best Regards,',
